Work backlog item PL-32 — drive the type-erasing casts in tests/ to zero.

WHAT DONE MEANS. Both ceilings in tests/sop/type-erasing-casts.ledger.json read 0
("as any" is 241 and "as never" is 190 as of 2026-09-02), and `npm run gate`
exits 0. Nothing else counts as done.

HOW TO PROVE IT EACH TURN. After every batch, run
`npx jest --no-coverage tests/sop/type-erasing-casts.test.ts > /tmp/casts.txt 2>&1`
and paste the two ceiling numbers it reports into your reply. Do not describe
progress in prose without those numbers — the evaluator reads only what you
surface, so an unpasted number does not exist.

METHOD. Read `.claude/skills/ask-the-tool/SKILL.md` first and use it: change many
sites at once, run `npm run typecheck:tests`, and let the compiler name the sites
where the cast was load-bearing. An ARGUMENT cast is a silenced type error, never
a formatting problem — build the object the callee declares instead of casting,
and if that is impossible, leave the cast and say why.

RULES. Lower the ledger ceiling to the new measurement after each batch; never
raise it. Commit each batch separately with a `Backlog: PL-32` trailer, and only
after `npm run gate` exits 0 — capture the exit code in a variable, never read it
through a pipe. Push after each commit. Make no cloud writes and no cross-item
changes.

STOP EARLY AND SAY SO if a remaining cast needs a product decision, or if two
consecutive batches fail the gate for the same reason. Also stop after 25 turns.
